0}], \"content\": \"one calendar year and from April 1, 1940, could be made only by individuals. Series E, F, and O have been on sale since May 1, 1941. Series E is a 10 year discount bond sold at 75% of maturity value, yielding 2.90% per annum if held to maturity; purchases are limited to $3,750 issue price in any one calendar year and may be made only by individuals. Series F is a 12 year discount bond sold at 74% of maturity value, yielding 2.53% per annum if held to maturity. Series O is a 12 year current income bond, sold at par, bearing interest at the rate of 2-1/2% per annum, redeemable at par on maturity, or at stated prices less than par before maturity. Purchase of Series F and O in any one calendar year are limited to $100,000 issue price for the two series combined ($50,000 in the calendar year 1941) and may be made by any investor other than commercial banks. 5/ Not yet available.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [751, 18, 803, 54], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"41\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [429, 94, 1122, 136], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Sales of United States Savings Bonds - (Continued)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [351, 145, 1217, 197], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Table 2.- Sales Reported by Series, Classified by Denomination\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [63, 206, 1506, 1636], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Fiscal year or month</th><th colspan=\\\"7\\\">Sales in millions of dollars at issue price</th><th colspan=\\\"7\\\">Percentage distribution of sales</th></tr><tr><th>Total all denominations</th><th>$25</th><th>$50</th><th>$100</th><th>$500</th><th>$1,000</th><th>$5,000</th><th>$10,000</th><th>Total all denominations</th><th>$25</th><th>$50</th><th>$100</th><th>$500