 are limited to $100,000 issue price for the two series combined ($50,000 in the calendar year 1941) and may be made by any investors other than commercial banks. For further details concerning redemption values and investment yields, see \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" for August 1943, page 4. 5/ Not yet available.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [745, 31, 776, 58], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"36\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [423, 103, 1098, 134], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Sales of United States Savings Bonds - (Continued)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [341, 157, 1184, 195], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Table 2.- Sales Reported by Series, Classified by Denomination\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [60, 235, 1453, 356], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Fiscal year or month</th><th colspan=\\\"7\\\">Sales in millions of dollars at issue price</th><th colspan=\\\"7\\\">Percentage distribution of sales</th></tr><tr><th>Total all denominations</th><th>$25</th><th>$50</th><th>$100</th><th>$500</th><th>$1,000</th><th>$5,000</th><th>$10,000</th><th>Total all denominations</th><th>$25</th><th>$50</th><th>$100</th><th>$500</th><th>$1,000</th><th>$5,000</th><th>$10,000</th></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [719, 365, 802, 388], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Series 3\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [62, 390, 1454, 807], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>1941 1/</td><td>203.1</td><td>14.4</td><td>13.3</td><td>41.4</td><td>40.7</td><td>93.4</td><td>.....</td><td>.....</td><td>100.0</td><td>7.1</td><td>6.5</td><td>20.4</td><td>20.0</td><td>46.0</td><td>.....</td><td