\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [591, 507, 601, 518], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [178, 576, 246, 590], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"LEGEND\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [147, 590, 163, 613], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [168, 595, 288, 613], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Under 100%\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [180, 622, 238, 639], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"100% to\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [245, 622, 288, 639], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"119%\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [176, 649, 242, 666], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"120% to\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [249, 647, 293, 668], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"139%\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 24, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [180, 678, 264, 696], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"140% or over\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 25, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [141, 676, 157, 693], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 26, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [346, 710, 712, 740], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"Including partnerships and personal trust accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 27, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [174, 786, 889, 850], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": \"SALES OF SERIES E SAVING BONDS IN 6TH WAR LOAN\\nPercent of Quota Reached in Each State\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 28, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [57, 840, 975, 1396], \"page_id\": 17}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 29, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [535, 24, 591, 46], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"A-10\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [881, 5, 1079, 44], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [52, 93, 537, 154], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Treasury bonds. State and local governments invested primarily in the 7/8% certificates and the 2% bonds.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [57, 159, 453, 207], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Subscriptions Under the Deferred Payment Plan\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [56, 207, 544, 428], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"The deferred payment plan allowed certain groups of investors through February 28, 1945 to make full payment for their subscriptions to the 8-10 year 2% Treasury bonds of 1952-54 and to the long-term 2-1/2% Treasury bonds of 1966-71. The securities themselves are delivered only as final payment is received. The investors permitted to use this plan were: life insurance companies, savings institutions, State and local governmen-tal units, and similar public corporations and agencies.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [57, 436, 544, 502], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"The table below shows subscriptions made under the deferred payment plan by investor classes and issues.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [52, 504, 537, 811], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Class of investor</th><th>Total</th><th>2-1/2% Treasury bonds</th><th>2% Treasury bonds</th><th>Not classified</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"5\\\">(In millions of dollars)</td></tr><tr><td>Savings banks</td><td>428</td><td>8</td><td>420</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance companies</td><td>432</td><td>249</td><td>151</td><td>32</td></tr><tr><td>State and local governments</td><td>76</td><td>27</td><td>49</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Savings and loan associations</td><td>43</td><td>6</td><td>34</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Fraternal benefit associations and other investors</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>1</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total</td><td>985</td><td>295</td><td>655</td><td>35</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [57, 819, 539, 947], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Sales to savings banks and insurance companies of $428 and $432 millions, respectively, accounted for the major part of subscriptions under this plan. Deferred payment subscriptions by these investor groups in the Sixth War Loan were about three times such sales in the Fifth Loan.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [61, 972, 260, 998], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Sales by States\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [52, 998, 544, 1196], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"The accompanying maps show the percentage of quotas reached during the Sixth War Loan in each of the States for (1) total sales, (2) sales to corporations and other investors, (3) sales to individuals, and (4) sales of Series E savings bonds. Table 2 compares the dollar value of sales with goals for the same categories in each State. For purposes of this discussion the District of Columbia and Northern and Southern California are counted as separate State units.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [58, 1206, 544, 1357], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Total sales and sales to corporations and other investors exceeded the goals in all the States (Map 1 and Map 2). Sales quotas for individuals (Map 3) were not reached in six of the States, namely, four New England States (Connecticut, Maine, Rhode Island and Vermont) and two Southern States (Florida and Georgia). Only one\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [582, 90, 1075, 227], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"State, Maryland, failed to achieve the sales quota for Series E savings bonds (Map 4). The record for sales to individuals in the Sixth War Loan, therefore, was much better than in the Fifth, when 16 States did not reach their sales goals for individuals and 10 States fell short in Series E bond sales.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [582, 241, 1071, 382], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Three States, Montana, North Dakota, and Wyoming exceeded their Series E sales goals by 50% or more. Seventeen States achieved 120% to 149% of their goals. Although, as mentioned above, all States but one reached their E bond quotas, the Western part of the country made a far better showing than the East.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 397, 1071, 480], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Among the territories and possessions, Alaska and Hawaii reached 154% and 142% of their E bond quotas respectively, thus ranking with the top four States.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 494, 1071, 847], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Table 3 supplies additional information on sales by States. In the table, sales to individuals in each State are broken down between Series E savings bonds, Series F and G savings bonds, and savings notes and marketable securities as a whole; total sales to each of the remaining investor classes are also shown for each State. As in prior war loans, the distribution of sales to insurance companies, savings banks, corporations and associations, savings and loan associations, and dealers and brokers largely reflects the concentration of the funds of these organizations in the various parts of the country. However, as noted above, the State distribution of sales to corporations was also affected by allocations of statistical credits from one State to another which were made by the Federal Reserve Banks in accordance with the wishes of subscribers.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [585, 858, 1071, 1004], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"A supplement to this article, and to the current \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\", is being prepared for early release and will be available upon request. This supplement will consist of additional tables on the Sixth War Loan showing by States the sales to each investor class, classified by type of issue.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 1008, 986, 1055], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Comparison of the Results of the Six War Loans\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [585, 1053, 1073, 1137], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"The distribution for the six war loans of total sales in dollar amounts and the percentage division of sales among the major investor groups is given in the table on page A-12.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [585, 1147, 1075, 1350], \"page_id\": 18}], \"content\": \"Sales in the six war loans aggregated $109 billions, of which nonbank investors accounted for $99 billions or 91%. Sales to individuals aggregated $28 billions or 25% of the total, while corporations and other investors accounted for $72 billions or 65%. Sales to commercial banks, which were included only in the first two war loans and then on a limited basis, amounted to $10 billions, or 9% of the total. As noted earlier, war loan sales figures represent gross\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 19, 213, 44], \"page_id\": 19}], \"content\": \"January 1945\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [560, 27, 600, 42], \"page_id\": 19}], \"content\": \"A-11\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [285, 66, 876, 120], \"page_id\": 19}], \"content\": \"GOALS AND SALES FOR SIX WAR LOANS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [468, 125, 686, 147], \"page_id\": 19}], \"content\": \"By Investor Classes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [92, 152, 1053, 1403], \"page_id\": 19}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [230, 1406, 660, 1420], \"page_id\": 19}], \"content\": \"Treasury investment accounts were included only in the first three war loans\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [229, 1420, 656, 1435], \"page_id\": 19}], \"content\": \"2/ Combined goal of $4 billion for all investors excluding commercial banks\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [229, 1435, 484, 1449], \"page_id\": 19}], \"content\": \"3/ No separate goal was set for Series E bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [230, 1450, 933, 1465], \"page_id\": 19}], \"content\": \"4 This figure represents the fixed amount which commercial banks were allowed to buy, rather than a goal for such investors\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [558, 32, 600, 48], \"page_id\": 20}], \"content\": \"A-12\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [916, 15, 1090, 49], \"page_id\": 20}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [77, 90, 552, 129], \"page_id\": 20}], \"content\": \"sales and do not indicate the net absorption of securities by investor classes.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [77, 134, 552, 426], \"page_id\": 20}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>War Loan</th><th>Total</th><th>Individuals</th><th>Corporations and other investors 1/</th><th>Commercial banks 2/</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"5\\\">Amounts in billions of dollars</td></tr><tr><td>First............</td><td>12.9</td><td>1.6</td><td>6.3</td><td>5.1</td></tr><tr><td>Second............</td><td>18.6</td><td>3.3</td><td>10.2</td><td>5.1</td></tr><tr><td>Third............</td><td>18.9</td><td>5.4</td><td>13.6</td><td>...</td></tr><tr><td>Fourth............</td><td>16.7</td><td>5.3</td><td>11.4</td><td>...</td></tr><tr><td>Fifth............</td><td>20.6</td><td>6.4</td><td>14.3</td><td>...</td></tr><tr><td>Sixth............</td><td>21.6</td><td>5.9</td><td>15.7</td><td>...</td></tr><tr><td>Total for six war loans....</td><td>109.4</td><td>27.8</td><td>71.5</td><td>10.2</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 426, 552, 614], \"page_id\": 20}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th colspan=\\\"4\\\">Percentage distribution</th></tr><tr><td>First.........</td><td>100.0</td><td>12.3</td><td>48.4</td><td>39.3</td></tr><tr><td>Second......</td><td>100.0</td><td>17.7</td><td>54.9</td><td>27.4</td></tr><tr><td>Third......</td><td>100.0</td><td>28.4</td><td>71.6</td><td>...</td></tr><tr><td>Fourth.....</td><td>100.0</td><td>31.7</td><td>68.3</td><td>...</td></tr><tr><td>Fifth......</td><td>100.0</td><td>30.8</td><td>69.2</td><td>...</td></tr><tr><td>Sixth......</td><td>100.0</td><td>27.2</td><td>72.8</td><td>...</td></tr><tr><td>Total for six war loans....</td><td>100.0</td><td>25.4</td><td>65.3</td><td>9.3</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [83, 611, 554, 745], \"page_id\": 20}], \"content\": \"1/ Treasury investment accounts were included in the first three war loans only; during succeeding war loans, sales to these accounts were handled outside of the drive.\\n2/ Commercial banks were allowed to buy only $5 billions of Federal securities during each of the first two war loans, and were excluded from direct participation in all later war loans.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [609, 90, 1083, 343], \"page_id\": 20}], \"content\": \"A comparison of sales with goals for each of the six war loans is given in Chart 4 for (1) all investors, (2) individuals, (3) corporations and other investors (excluding commercial banks), and (4) commercial banks (included only during the first two war loans). Table 4 gives a historical analysis of sales of securities by investor classes and by issues for each war loan. Details on the sales goals and dates relating to the six drives are presented in Table 5. Table 6 gives for Series E bonds the dollar value and the number of units of each denomination sold during each of the six drives.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [609, 363, 1077, 431], \"page_id\": 20}], \"content\": \"Note: In accordance with customary Bulletin practice, all figures in this article have been rounded and will not necessarily add to totals. Percentages, in all cases, have been calculated from unrounded figures.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 30, 228, 68], \"page_id\": 21}], \"content\": \"January 1945\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [561, 39, 608, 64], \"page_id\": 21}], \"content\": \"A-13\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [273, 88, 891, 151], \"page_id\": 21}], \"content\": \"Table 1.- Sales of Securities in the Sixth War Loan, by Classes of Investors and by Issues\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"},