d be used in payment of each class of tax (income, estate or gift) by each taxpayer during each taxable year was limited to 45 per cent of the total tax payable for that year. In 1943, Series B notes were sold from August 1, 1941 through September 12, 1942, to yield approximately 0.45% per annum. The amount which may be turned in on taxes is unlimited. The notes may be redeemed for cash only at the original purchase price. Series C notes went on sale September 14, 1942. Interest accrues each month on a graduated scale (see \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" for August 1943, page 4) to yield approximately 1.07% per annum if held to maturity. These notes may be used in payment of Federal taxes at any time two months after the date of issue. The amount which may be used in payment of taxes is limited to 45 per cent of the cash six months after the date of issue at the tax payment value current at the time of presentation. Prior to July 27, 1943, notice of 30 days was required for cash redemption. See also footnote 1.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [575, 36, 593, 51], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"42\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [923, 27, 1092, 54], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [358, 95, 807, 115], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"Sales of Treasury Savings Notes - (Continued)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [269, 132, 898, 148], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"Table 2.- Sales of Series C Notes, Classified by Denomination\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [60, 178, 1110, 662], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Fiscal year or month</th><th colspan=\\\"10\\\">Sales in millions of dollars at par</th><th colspan=\\\"1