ds are computed on the basis of the mean of closing bid and ask quotations in the over-the-counter market, beginning September 2, 1941; previously, closing prices on the New York Stock Exchange were based on days when sales took place on the Exchange in a particular issue and the mean of closing bid and ask quotations on the New York Stock Exchange on days when no sales took place. (2) Corporate bond yields are computed on the basis of closing prices on the New York Stock Exchange and the New York Curb Exchange; on days when an issue does not sell, the value of the last regular sale is used. Back Figure: Monthly and weekly data for the period January 1933 through March 1944 may be found in the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" for April 1944, pages 57-61. Revised 1/4 Average of Treasury bonds neither due nor callable for fifteen years. For discussion of composition of average see \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" for March 1944, page 58. Partially tax-exempt bonds are those the interest on which is exempt from the normal rates of the Federal income tax, except that in the case of partially tax-exempt\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [625, 1067, 1102, 1330], \"page_id\": 83}], \"content\": \"Treasury and United States earning bonds, interest derived from $5,000 of principal amount owned by any one holder is also exempt from the surtax rates of the Federal income tax. Taxable bonds are those the interest on which is subject to both the normal and surtax rates of the Federal income tax. For discussion of present composition of high-grade corporate bond average, see the article appearing on page 56 of this issue; for discussion of its previous composition, as well as the considerations underlying its construction, see \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" for April 1943, page 61. Monthly averages of daily figures. Prior to April 1, 1938, corporate bonds are averages of Saturday figures. The composition of the high-grade corporate bond average was revised commencing with November 1, 1944. See article on page 56 of this issue. On days when the exchanges are closed, the date and prices of the previous day are used. Indicates change in composition of average. Exchange closed.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [610, 36, 632, 51], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"58\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [958, 15, 1145, 54], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [110, 273, 141, 1282], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"AVERAGE YIELDS OF LONG-TERM TREASURY AND CORPORATE BONDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 696, 170, 870], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"Monthly Series\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 54, 1150, 1467], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [61, 32, 202, 54], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"January 1945\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [553, 34, 574, 51], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"59\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [198, 696, 922, 749], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"CORPORATIONS AND CREDIT AGENCIES OF THE UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [580, 41, 598, 54], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"60\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [927, 25, 1099, 54], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [200, 93, 993, 114], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Sources and A